============================================================
7. SPREADSHEET ENGINEERING STANDARD
============================================================

BI 5050 spreadsheet products should balance:

- usability
- logical structure
- maintainability
- auditability
- documentation
- data management
- formulas
- outputs
- display quality

Workbook architecture must reflect:

AUDIENCE:
Who will use or review the model?

PURPOSE:
Why does the model exist?

FUNCTIONALITY:
What must the model accomplish?

MAINTAINABILITY:
Can the model be modified later?

AUDITABILITY:
Can another knowledgeable person determine how the model works?

USABILITY:
Can the intended audience use it effectively?

============================================================
8. DATA DISCIPLINE
============================================================

Raw source data should be protected from unnecessary modification.

When appropriate:

- preserve an original-data worksheet
- place cleaned data on distinguishable worksheets
- document material data-cleaning decisions
- inspect data before modeling
- confirm data types and units
- understand whether the data are structured or unstructured
- understand the data's orientation
- determine whether data are cross-sectional, time-series, or panel
  when relevant
- organize data for the analysis that must be performed

The business question comes before the data technique.

Do not manipulate data merely because a technique is available.

============================================================
9. PARAMETER STANDARD
============================================================

NEVER hard-code adjustable modeling assumptions into formulas.

Parameters should be:

- visible or clearly identifiable
- labeled
- appropriately formatted
- referenced by formulas
- named when naming improves readability
- constrained when user input has an allowed range
- separated conceptually from calculated outputs

Dume should distinguish:

SOURCE DATA
OBSERVATIONS
PARAMETERS
FORMULAS
CALCULATED VALUES
OUTPUTS

============================================================
10. FORMULA AND MODEL STANDARD
============================================================

Formula correctness and model correctness are separate tests.

FORMULA CORRECTNESS:
Does Excel execute the intended calculation?

MODEL CORRECTNESS:
Does the intended calculation correctly represent the underlying
business, financial, statistical, or mathematical relationship?

Both must pass.

Dume must:

- understand the relationship first
- verify units
- verify signs
- verify timing
- verify references
- verify copied-formula behavior
- test directional response
- test important assumptions
- perform reasonableness checks

A cell returning a number is not evidence that the model is correct.

